  "body": "Run 43766509853 on main 17a8c6e76 failed. Only step [08] (app suites) failed. All other suites and clippy are green.\nThe failing test is `troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` in `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs`.\n\nEvidence:\n- The test asserts each message stem quoted on `site/content/guide/reference/troubleshooting.md` exists in `crates/*/src`.\n- One stem is no longer present: `model '<model>' was imported incomplete - closed shell`.\n- Cause: commit 35b3422cf (fix(import): load a STEP closed shell that meshes open as an incomplete model) reworded the message. The runtime text now reads `\"imported incomplete - {hole} - so it has walls missing...\"` (`crates/app/src/mesh_open.rs:75`). The old literal moved to a test file (`crates/app/tests/import_step_open_shell.rs:38`), which the guard does not scan.\n- The previous batch runs on earlier main commits were cancelled (merge storm), so this guard gap is latent since that commit merged.\n\nFix direction (choose one, keep it small):\n- Update the `### ` heading stem on the troubleshooting page to quote a literal that exists in `crates/*/src`, or\n- Re-add a literal form of the message in `crates/app/src/mesh_open.rs`.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting` passes on main, and the next post-merge run is green.\n\nReported by: SlaveSession (the workflow report job is still broken, #1611).\n",
